cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QCell: a quantum-to-cellular multiscale model of an intracellular biosensor"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sadhukhan
    given-names: Jhuma
    affiliation: "University of Surrey"
    email: j.sadhukhan@surrey.ac.uk
repository-code: "https://github.com/jhumasadhukhan/qcell-multiscale"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation coupling a first-principles excitonic layer
  (electronic coupling, orientation factor, cytoplasmic refractive index and
  band-resolved optical transport) to a dynamic model of polyhydroxyalkanoate
  fermentation fed with bioelectrochemical formate. Demonstrates that a
  ratiometric FRET readout is not self-calibrating in a granule-accumulating
  culture, and supplies the correction.
keywords:
  - multiscale modelling
  - FRET biosensor
  - polyhydroxyalkanoate
  - bioprocess control
  - Foerster resonance energy transfer
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Polymer accumulation biases the intracellular biosensor used to control it"
  authors:
    - family-names: Sadhukhan
      given-names: Jhuma
  year: 2026
